Subject: A stack object moves to the heap by taking over its shape reference and fields

What this does
  - `js_stack_migrate2` (the move of a stack object, and the stack object a field of it holds, to the heap) has a path for the case without a stack Array: each heap object is allocated with the room `qjs_aot_new_from_shape_cap` would give it, then takes the block's shape reference (no duplicate, no release), copies the block's fields once, leaves the block's fields undefined and its shape NULL (the state `qjs_aot_stack_release` leaves), and a field that held the child holds the heap child. The slot-claim check (`qjs_aot_object_filled`) runs as before.
  - `QJS_AOT_NOMIGFAST=1` in the run's environment selects the old path in a kit build (QJS_KIT_TEST_KNOBS); the production build has neither the read nor the per-field check of the moved fields.

Why we need it
  A move cost 1,196 instructions in raytrace (two allocations that initialise every slot and are then overwritten, two release walks over the fields, a child test on every property, a shape duplicate and a release); it is now about 820, of which the claim check is a third. 117k moves per 10 runs.

Failure
  Out of memory in either allocation returns 0 with nothing moved, as before (the second failure frees the first object). Objects with more fields than the inline limit take the old path.

Soundness
  - The block's shape reference is transferred, so the shape's count is unchanged; the block ends with the NULL shape every consumer of a migrated block already sees.
  - Both heap objects are allocated before anything is moved; the child's reference count is 1 for the caller plus one for the field of the parent that held it, as in the old path.
  - The object is linked into the collector's list only after its shape and fields are in place.
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -67110,0 +67111,68 @@
+#ifdef QJS_KIT_TEST_KNOBS
+static bool getenv_nomigfast(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+    if (unlikely(v < 0))
+        v = getenv("QJS_AOT_NOMIGFAST") != NULL;
+    return v;
+}
+#else
+#define getenv_nomigfast() false
+#endif
+
+/* The heap object a stack block moves to, in two steps so that a failure leaves every block as it was. The first allocates it with the room qjs_aot_new_from_shape_cap would give (the
+   fields past the block's own are undefined); the second takes the block's shape reference (no duplicate, no release) and its fields, leaves the block's fields undefined and its shape
+   NULL as qjs_aot_stack_release does, and links the object into the collector's list. */
+static JSObject *js_aot_moved_alloc(JSContext *ctx, JSObject *src)
+{
+    JSRuntime *rt = ctx->rt;
+    JSShape *sh = src->shape;
+    uint32_t n = sh->prop_count, cap = js_aot_inline_room(sh, src->prop_inline_cap), i;
+    JSObject *h;
+    JSProperty *pr;
+    js_trigger_gc(rt, sizeof(JSObject));
+    h = js_malloc(ctx, offsetof(JSObject, u) + cap * sizeof(JSProperty));
+    if (unlikely(!h))
+        return NULL;
+    h->prop_inline_cap = cap;
+    h->class_id = JS_CLASS_OBJECT;
+    h->values_inline = 0;
+    h->arr_kind = JS_ARR_KIND_GENERIC;
+    h->extensible = true;
+    h->free_mark = 0;
+    h->is_exotic = 0;
+    h->fast_array = 0;
+    h->holey = 0;
+    h->is_constructor = 0;
+    h->is_uncatchable_error = 0;
+    h->tmp_mark = 0;
+    h->is_HTMLDDA = 0;
+    h->gv_watched = 0;
+    h->is_prototype = 0;
+    h->first_weak_ref = NULL;
+    pr = (JSProperty *)((uint8_t *)h + offsetof(JSObject, u));
+    h->prop = pr;
+    for (i = n; i < cap; i++)
+        pr[i].u.value = JS_UNDEFINED;
+    JS_REF_COUNT(h) = 1;
+    return h;
+}
+static void js_aot_moved_fill(JSContext *ctx, JSObject *h, JSObject *src, JSObject *child, JSValue hchild)
+{
+    JSShape *sh = src->shape;
+    int i, n = sh->prop_count;
+    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        JSValue v = src->prop[i].u.value;
+        if (child != NULL && JS_VALUE_HAS_REF_COUNT(v) && JS_VALUE_GET_PTR(v) == (void *)child)
+            v = JS_DupValue(ctx, hchild);
+#ifdef QJS_KIT_TEST_KNOBS
+        assert(JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(v) != JS_TAG_OBJECT || JS_REF_COUNT(JS_VALUE_GET_OBJ(v)) < JS_STACK_BIAS / 2);   /* the region's analysis keeps at most the one stack child in a field */
+#endif
+        h->prop[i].u.value = v;
+        src->prop[i].u.value = JS_UNDEFINED;
+    }
+    h->shape = sh;
+    src->shape = NULL;
+    add_gc_object(ctx->rt, &h->header, JS_GC_OBJ_TYPE_JS_OBJECT);
+}
+
